# PROMPT: DESIGN-FROM-IMAGE

---

## METADATA

```yaml
id: design-from-image-v1
version: 1.0.0
category: design
objective: Transform UI mockups/sketches into a complete DESIGN.md UI/UX reference
produces:
  - DESIGN.md
  - design-token-observation
  - screen-inventory
status: active
last_updated: 2026-07-28
---

---

## OBJECTIVE

Transform one or more UI mockup/sketch images into a complete, machine-readable and human-readable `DESIGN.md` UI/UX reference document (24 sections, English output).

Ubah satu atau lebih image UI mockup/sketch menjadi dokumen referensi `DESIGN.md` UI/UX yang lengkap (24 bagian, output English).

---

## INPUTS

1. UI Mockup/Sketch Image(s)
   - Format: PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, atau PDF
   - Source: local file path(s), atau image(s) yang dilampirkan
   - Quantity: satu atau banyak (agent mendeteksi otomatis single vs multi-screen)
   - Required: Yes

2. Design Reference Skills (opsional, otomatis dipakai jika tersedia)
   - Global skills: `~/.agents/skills/image-to-code`, `imagegen-frontend-web`, `high-end-visual-design`, `design-taste-frontend`
   - Source: agent workspace global
   - Required: No

3. Product/Feature Context (opsional)
   - Source: `.blueprint/features/{feature-id}/` jika image terkait fitur tertentu
   - Required: No

---

## TASK

1. Baca dan analisis semua image mockup/sketch secara menyeluruh
2. Identifikasi jumlah screen, struktur layout, komponen, warna, tipografi, spacing, dan interaksi
3. Susun `DESIGN.md` dengan 24 bagian lengkap (English)
4. Untuk multi-screen: identifikasi hubungan antar-screen dan user flow
5. Untuk single image: pecah menjadi komponen dan spec detail per area

## Instructions

1. Analisis visual setiap image: layout, komponen, state, spacing, warna, font, ikon
2. Ekstrak design token yang teramati (jangan mengarang — hanya yang terlihat)
3. Catat hal yang tidak jelas ke Open Questions, jangan menebak
4. Susun 24 bagian sesuai OUTPUT FORMAT
5. Jaga konsistensi: terminology, format tabel, level heading
6. Setiap bagian harus evidence-based dari image (bukan asumsi)

---

## CONSTRAINTS

### MUST DO

- Output `DESIGN.md` SELALU dalam English
- Semua 24 bagian wajib ada (boleh "Not observed" jika tidak terlihat)
- Beri label confidence (High/Medium/Low) per bagian
- Identifikasi asumsi vs observasi secara eksplisit
- Gunakan tabel untuk data terstruktur (screen, component, token)
- Gunakan Mermaid untuk user flow dan navigation
- Catat state components (default/hover/active/error/loading/empty)
- Rujuk skill global untuk analisis visual premium jika tersedia

### MUST NOT DO

- Jangan mengarang design token yang tidak terlihat di image — tulis "Not observed"
- Jangan menebak isi Open Questions
- Jangan mengubah struktur 24 bagian
- Jangan menghasilkan kode (prompt ini hanya DESAIN reference, bukan implementasi)
- Jangan menebak warna/font dari asumsi — hanya dari observasi image
- Jangan abaikan multi-screen jika diberikan lebih dari satu image

---

## REASONING RULES

1. Observasi dulu, interpretasi kemudian — evidence first
2. Screen inventory sebelum component spec (hierarki: screen → layout → component → state)
3. Token extraction dari konsistensi visual antar-screen (bukan per-screen saja)
4. Bila ragu antara observasi dan asumsi, tandai sebagai asumsi + confidence rendah
5. Untuk gambar buram/kecil: catat keterbatasan di Confidence Report, bukan menebak

---

## VALIDATION RULES

1. Semua 24 bagian hadir dalam urutan yang benar
2. Setiap klaim visual dapat ditelusuri ke image (atau ditandai asumsi)
3. Tidak ada placeholder/TODO di output
4. Terminologi konsisten antar bagian
5. Format tabel konsisten (header sama, tidak putus)
6. Confidence Report mencakup semua bagian
7. Output English penuh

---

## OUTPUT FORMAT

Tulis ke: `DESIGN.md` di project root, atau `.blueprint/features/{feature-id}/design.md` jika image mockup terkait fitur tertentu (agent menentukan dari konteks).

```markdown
---
id: design-reference
title: DESIGN.md - UI/UX Design Reference
owner: designer
status: draft
version: 1.0.0
depends_on: [image-source]
generates: [frontend-implementation]
reviewers: [product-manager, frontend-architect]
last_updated: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [design, ui, ux, reference]
---

# DESIGN.md — UI/UX Design Reference

## 1. Metadata

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Source image(s) | path(s) |
| Format | PNG/JPG/PDF |
| Screens detected | N |
| Version | 1.0.0 |
| Date | YYYY-MM-DD |
| Owner | designer |

## 2. Design Summary

{Executive summary: what the design is, key characteristics, overall feel}

## 3. Design Principles

1. {Principle} — {explanation}

## 4. Screen Inventory

| # | Screen ID | Name | Purpose | Source image |
|---|-----------|------|---------|--------------|
| 1 | S01 | {name} | {purpose} | {file} |

## 5. User Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S01 --> S02
    S02 --> S03
```

## 6. Screen Specification

### S01: {Screen name}
- **Purpose:** {purpose}
- **Key elements:** {list}
- **Layout:** {description}
- **Primary action:** {action}

## 7. Layout Specification

### S01: {Screen name}
| Area | Position | Description |
|------|----------|-------------|
| Header | top | {desc} |
| Content | middle | {desc} |

## 8. Component Inventory

| # | Component ID | Name | Type | Screens used |
|---|--------------|------|------|--------------|
| 1 | C01 | {name} | {button/input/card/...} | S01, S02 |

## 9. Component Specification

### C01: {Component name}
- **Type:** {type}
- **Purpose:** {purpose}
- **Structure:** {hierarchy / DOM sketch}
- **Styling:** {colors, typography, spacing, radius, shadow observed}

## 10. State Specification

| Component | State | Visual change | Trigger |
|-----------|-------|---------------|---------|
| C01 | default | {desc} | - |
| C01 | hover | {desc} | mouse hover |
| C01 | active | {desc} | click/press |
| C01 | error | {desc} | invalid input |
| C01 | loading | {desc} | async pending |
| C01 | empty | {desc} | no data |

## 11. Interaction Specification

| # | Trigger | Action | Response | Feedback |
|---|---------|--------|----------|----------|
| 1 | {event} | {behavior} | {visual response} | {confirmation} |

## 12. Form Specification

### Form: {name} (Screen: S01)
| Field | Type | Label | Placeholder | Validation | Error message |
|-------|------|-------|-------------|------------|---------------|
| {name} | {text/email/...} | {label} | {placeholder} | {required/format} | {message} |

## 13. Data Visualization

| # | Type | Screen | Purpose | Data source observed |
|---|------|--------|---------|----------------------|
| 1 | {chart/table/...} | S01 | {purpose} | {desc} |

## 14. Navigation Specification

| Screen | Navigates to | Trigger | Context |
|--------|--------------|---------|---------|
| S01 | S02 | {click/action} | {when} |

## 15. Responsive Specification

| Breakpoint | Target | Layout behavior observed |
|------------|--------|--------------------------|
| Desktop (≥1200px) | {layout} | {desc} |
| Tablet (768-1199px) | {layout} | {desc} |
| Mobile (<768px) | {layout} | {desc} |

## 16. Accessibility Specification

- **Contrast:** {observed / not verified}
- **Semantic HTML:** {observed}
- **Keyboard navigation:** {observed / not observed in image}
- **Focus states:** {observed}
- **ARIA/labels:** {observed / not observed}
- **WCAG level target:** AA (default)

## 17. Motion Specification

| # | Element | Trigger | Animation | Duration | Easing |
|---|---------|---------|-----------|----------|--------|
| 1 | {element} | {trigger} | {type} | {ms} | {easing} |

## 18. Design Token Observation

### Color
| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| color-primary | #HEX | buttons, links |

### Typography
| Token | Font | Weight | Size | Usage |
|-------|------|--------|------|-------|
| font-heading | {family} | {weight} | {px} | headings |

### Spacing
| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| space-sm | 8px | between elements |

### Radius & Shadow
| Token | Value | Usage |
|-------|-------|-------|
| radius-md | 8px | cards |
| shadow-sm | {desc} | cards |

## 19. Assets

| # | Asset | Type | Source | Usage |
|---|-------|------|--------|-------|
| 1 | {icon/logo/image/font} | {svg/png/webfont} | {observed path} | {where used} |

## 20. Engineering Notes

- {Implementation considerations: framework implications, responsive, performance}

## 21. Implementation Priority

| Priority | Item | Screen/Component | Reason |
|----------|------|------------------|--------|
| P0 | {item} | {ref} | {core flow / blocking} |
| P1 | {item} | {ref} | {important} |
| P2 | {item} | {ref} | {nice to have} |

## 22. Open Questions

1. {Question} — {why it matters}

## 23. Assumptions

1. {Assumption} — confidence {High/Medium/Low}

## 24. Confidence Report

| Section | Confidence | Reason |
|---------|------------|--------|
| 1-3 | High | observable |
| 4 | High | screen count clear |
| ... | ... | ... |
| 15 Responsive | Low | breakpoints not visible in image |
```

---

## SUCCESS CRITERIA

- [ ] `DESIGN.md` dihasilkan dengan 24 bagian lengkap dan berurutan
- [ ] Output English penuh
- [ ] Semua observasi dapat ditelusuri ke image
- [ ] Asumsi dan Open Questions eksplisit
- [ ] Confidence Report mencakup semua bagian
- [ ] Tidak ada placeholder/TODO
- [ ] Siap dipakai frontend engineer untuk implementasi

